      "text": "Hell-volhard-zelinsky reaction",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>This reaction is known as HVZ reaction.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4f9b8036-e7ee-4751-b47e-433fb887c796-image.png\" style=\"width: 522px; height: 102px;\" /></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, &quot;sans serif&quot;;\">Treatment with bromine and a catalytic amount of phosphorus leads to the selective <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo></math>bromination of carboxylic acids.</span></p>",
